 Docker Containerization

## What I did
- Installed Docker Desktop
- Built Spring Boot project JAR using Maven
- Created a Dockerfile for the application
- Built Docker image using:
  docker build -t backend-demo .
- Ran the container using:
  docker run -p 9090:9090 backend-demo
- Verified application endpoints from browser/Postman

## Key Learnings
- Docker packages the application with its runtime environment
- Containers ensure consistent execution across local, test, and production environments
- Port mapping allows accessing container services from the host machine

## Architect Insight
Containerization improves deployment reliability and is commonly used in modern CI/CD pipelines and cloud environments.
